  "id": "DrugBank_DB00954 - MONDO_21680",
  "verbalization": "Dirithromycin is associated with Streptococcal Infection through a chain of indications that link it to bacterial infections. The evidence suggests that Dirithromycin may be used to treat a range of bacterial infections, including Streptococcal Pneumonia and Pneumonia, which in turn are indicated to be treated by Cefdinir and Cefonicid, respectively. These antibiotics are commonly used in the management of Streptococcal Infections, indicating a potential pathway where Dirithromycin could contribute to the treatment of such infections through its antibacterial activity. The overlapping indications suggest that Dirithromycin may be a viable alternative or adjunct in the treatment of Streptococcal Infections, particularly in cases where other antibiotics are not effective. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Dirithromycin to play a role in the treatment of Streptococcal Infections, though further studies are needed to confirm its efficacy and mechanisms of action in this context.",
